        rules: {
          objective: 'Earn the most points from legal goods, contraband, bonuses, and remaining coins after everyone has served as sheriff equally.',
          gameplay: 'Players draw and discard goods cards, secretly load goods into bags, declare a legal good type and quantity, then negotiate with the current sheriff. The sheriff may allow a bag through or inspect it; truthful players are compensated if inspected, while liars lose undeclared goods and pay penalties.',
          keyRules: [
            'Players may lie about goods type but must state the correct number of cards.',
            'The sheriff rotates each round.',
            'Bribes and promises are part of the negotiation loop.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus first on the visible objective in Sheriff of Nottingham: conserve cards or resources that directly advance the win condition.',
          intermediate: 'Track public information and avoid giving opponents easy tempo swings during the middle turns.',
          advanced: 'Plan several turns ahead around the scoring window and force opponents into low-value or defensive plays.',
